AB  - The rise of Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen AI) tools is changing the way students at higher education institutions access and use information, particularly in developing countries in Africa. This study investigated the perception and usage of university students toward traditional library services in the context of the increasing adoption of Gen AI. guided by the Technology Acceptance Model (TAM), the study aimed to assess awareness, use, perceptions, extent of use, and factors shaping students' preferences between AI tools and library resources. A cross-sectional descriptive design was employed, involving 323 university students from Nigeria, Ghana, Botswana, and South Africa. Data were collected via an online questionnaire and analyzed using descriptive and inferential statistics. The findings revealed moderate awareness and uneven use of Gen AI tools across disciplines, with students in science and technology fields reporting higher engagement. Although most students found Gen AI more accessible and convenient, they continued to recognize the value of libraries in terms of credibility, structure, and human support. However, declining library patronage signals an urgent need for libraries to evolve through digital integration and the adoption of AI-enabled services. This study concludes that, while libraries in developing countries remain essential, they must reposition themselves as partners in AI-driven learning by embedding AI literacy, ethical guidance, and digital adaptability into their service delivery. The study recommends that universities in these countries strengthen AI literacy by encouraging ethical, critical, and metacognitive engagement with a plethora of Gen AI tools across curricula, learning management systems, and library services. Academic libraries should be strategically repositioned as central hubs for AI education and digital transformation, supported by clear institutional guidelines and faculty-led training to promote responsible and trustworthy AI-enabled academic practice.
